WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:07.310
The 666th Squadron's role in Operation 
Neptune is almost complete.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:13.880
As you know, our squadron played 
a huge role in this mission.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.050
This was only possible because 
of our pilots' gallantry

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.880
and the dedicated work of our mechanics.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.600
Former Polish People's Republic Territory 
Gdansk

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.850
As your squadron commander, I thank you.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.830
Good work, everyone.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.360
Baltic Sea, Off the Coast of Bornholm  
TSF Landing Craft <i>Peenemunde</i>

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.290
It's over, Brother.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.050
You'd barely had any time with 
us before the mission,

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.620
but you did great.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:32.630
To be honest, I was really scared.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.220
When I think of you going away again...

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.310
Someday, I'll be a great pilot like you.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.050
So, for now, let me cling to you a little longer.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:45.490
Lise...

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.560
I'll get right to the point.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:52.240
What's your opinion of Hohenstein?

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.380
She's not a dog of the Stasi.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.320
If she were...

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.050
She wouldn't risk her life to save the squadron?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:04.830
It could be an act.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.300
She won't betray me.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:10.330
She's still my sister, and that hasn't changed.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:15.990
Roger that.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:17.840
This is the last time we'll discuss this.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.170
We still don't believe you.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.310
The situation doesn't allow for that.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.340
The situation?

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.820
We can't tell anyone this yet, but...

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.570
The Minsk hive in Belarus has activated.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.770
Over a hundred thousand?

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.480
No way!

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.230
That's more than double Operation Neptune!

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.200
This battle will determine 
the fate of our Fatherland.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.700
So we have to use Lise?

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.540
That's not all.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.500
Several officers of the National People's 
Army have been arrested by the Stasi.

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:58.040
They're under suspicion of conspiracy 
and an attempted coup d'état.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.010
The party is asking the 
NPA to take responsibility.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.760
Supposedly, Command is in a panic 
trying to deal with it.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.890
The Stasi now completely has the 
upper hand. In the worst case...

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.440
They could take control of the military.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:17.090
If that happens, we'll be disbanded immediately.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.190
That's just the worst case scenario.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:25.450
The success of Operation Neptune 
has proven our value.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.700
If they disband us without any valid reason,

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.600
they could make enemies out of the West.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.590
They shouldn't want to try that.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.780
All forces, stand by!

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.460
All forces, stand by!

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.950
Battle stations!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.540
Theodor, TSFs!

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.510
Cheburashkas?

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.850
The Stasi?

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.500
The Werewolf Battalion?

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:00.820
No.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.070
Heinze... Heinze Axmann!

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.830
The Stasi officer who interrogated 
me three years ago.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.590
What do you want?

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.040
It would seem you don't like them, Iris.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.320
The Stasi's new TSF battalion, Berlin.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.600
We have come to celebrate 
your triumphant return.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.100
Captain Irisdina Bernhard,

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:38.080
you are under arrest for making 
counterrevolutionary statements

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.610
during Operation Neptune.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.820
You plan to start a fight with the 
military at a time like this?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.970
Who can say?

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.800
You are Second Lieutenant Lise Hohenstein?

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.330
Y-Yes.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:01.610
A tragic pair of siblings whose parents were 
purged for seeking asylum in the West.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:05.050
The older brother is a hero 
of Operation Neptune...

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:10.090
And you, the little sister, are a Stasi spy.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.720
That is the rumor.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.150
I'm not a spy!

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:23.130
Once an organization gets too big, 
it's hard to know who is working for it.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:26.310
Did one of my men send you here?

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.520
N-No, I...

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.500
Who would trust you?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.070
Everyone suspects you of being a dog.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:34.280
No!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.200
That's not...

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:41.460
Please stop these lies, 
Comrade Lieutenant Colonel!

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.620
What proof—

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.960
Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:49.780
have you ever thought about why you 
were the only one who was released?

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:57.230
What if someone sold themselves out 
to the Stasi in order to save you?

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.790
It is only a hypothesis,

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.330
but if you were released because of her,

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.940
would that not make sense?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:11.440
You'll have to fight with a spy in your midst.

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.570
But perhaps I can find out who hired her,

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:18.080
and free her.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.580
And in exchange, we work for you?

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.940
I think there is something in it for both of us.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:28.300
Lieutenant Colonel Axmann...

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:29.810
What?

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:34.780
We are soldiers who've sworn our 
loyalty to the party and the NPA.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.260
And Lise is an irreplaceable part of us,

00:07:38.260 --> 00:07:39.960
and a part of my family.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.600
She's not a spy!

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.600
Brother...

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.110
Truly beautiful.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.220
I shall be on my way.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.640
This was an interesting little farce.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.120
Iris, will you be coming with me?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.090
Yes, sir.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:08.500
Lise!

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:11.760
Brother, I...

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:13.400
I know.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:14.760
I know.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.020
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.020
Welcome back!

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.390
Sis!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.020
Welcome back!

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.480
Isn't this amazing?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.820
So many brand new Balalaikas.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.820
The whole squadron's getting 
lots of new equipment!

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.950
We need to understand why we're getting 
so much equipment right now.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:42.860
The BETA are coming, aren't they?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.880
More than a hundred thousand, right?

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.950
It doesn't seem real.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:50.560
With the West being so useless,

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:53.910
we need to be the shield 
that protects humanity.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.210
Um, Comrade Lieutenant?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.330
Isn't the USSR going to help us?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:01.680
They were the leader of 
the socialist countries.

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:07.810
Did you forget our history with 
them during the Cold War?

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:13.280
Well, history isn't my best subject...

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:17.660
USSR forces were stationed 
in East Germany, right?

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.860
East Germany, on the boundary 
between East and West,

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.660
was an important strategic point.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.530
In exchange for military support and supplies,

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:27.170
the USSR was allowed to station forces here.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:30.670
We were used, and abused, as convenient tools.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.910
That's what I learned in the West.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.660
M-Me, too! Maybe...

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.430
Sheesh...

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.310
Whatever.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.970
The Stasi are still connected to the KGB.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.990
If we ask for help, we'll end up 
completely under their control.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:50.770
But isn't that strange?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:51.360
What?

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:57.130
If the Stasi are connected to the USSR, 
shouldn't that have already happened?

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.570
Come to think of it, you're right.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:02.620
Even if they are closely connected,

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.560
the Stasi wouldn't discard what they 
have to work with the Soviets...

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:08.710
Wait... Is that it?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:28.310
Axmann asked me if we wanted a war with him.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.750
He seems insistent on bringing us over.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.050
He's panicking.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:33.770
Yes.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:35.480
What do you mean?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.160
A power struggle is happening within the Stasi.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:44.410
The Political HQ was aware of this.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:49.620
A Moscow faction connected to the KGB 
wants closer ties with the Soviets.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.800
The Minister of the Stasi, 
Major General Erich Schmidt,

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:58.200
and Beatrix Brehme, Commander of the 
Werewolf Battalion, lead the faction.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.970
They hold the majority within the Stasi.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:03.900
And Heinz Axmann's Berlin faction

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:08.350
wants to eliminate the Soviet influence, 
limiting relationships with the West

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.480
to maintain our national sovereignty.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:12.900
With the military no longer a threat,

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.110
the Moscow faction's only 
enemy is the Berlin faction.

00:11:17.290 --> 00:11:20.990
That's why Axmann wants us on 
his side to help fight a war?

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:22.690
That's terrible.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.840
Do they really plan on starting 
a war between East Germans?

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:29.280
Do they only care about their own power,

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.930
and not what happens to the people?!

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:34.890
For us to stop that from happening...

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:38.630
Lieutenant Jeckeln, 
Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:41.170
I have a request.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:49.430
East Berlin 
Defense Ministry Strategic HQ

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:51.390
You want us to raise the 666th's 
rank to "instructional squad"?

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:56.900
After this last mission, the 666th Squadron 
has become heroes to both East and West.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:59.570
By allowing us to conduct tactical training,

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:04.530
the military's value will increase and 
the Stasi will be unable to crush us.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.430
I want you to go to Berlin tomorrow 
and find cooperators.

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:10.290
Me, too?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.150
You are the hero who saved Gdansk.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.500
Just having you there will 
add much to her words.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:23.500
If we offer laserjagd know-how,

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.510
I think it will be easier to get the West's help.

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.310
You're a little too late.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:33.850
Political HQ has been putting pressure 
on us to reorganize the military.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:36.810
I believe the Stasi to be responsible.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.820
And you plan on giving in to that 
pressure, Comrade Major?

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.790
What else can I do?

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.950
I'm just a soldier.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:53.180
March 21st, 1981.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:58.380
You sold a number of artworks you acquired 
during the withdrawal from Poland

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.010
to the Russian mafia, didn't you?

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.920
Over 150,000 Marks' worth.

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.890
Those transactions were completely illegal.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.140
C-Comrade Lieutenant!

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.590
We're ready to send the documents 
to Political HQ if necessary.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.650
Please give us your decision, Comrade Major.

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.740
Not bad.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:28.410
That's a tactic everyone learns, 
if they want to advance in this country.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.040
Do you like this country?

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:36.730
I do.

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.260
The idea of socialism...

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.500
The peaceful town of Berlin...

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:49.010
I want to protect East Germany 
and the ideals it strives for.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:52.140
For that, I'd do anything.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.730
Okay, let's hurry to the next place.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:58.650
Next up is Lieutenant Colonel Augenthaler 
at the political commissioners...

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:01.440
Wh-What are you doing?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:01.990
Shh!

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.450
We're being followed.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.240
This way.

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.670
Sorry to scare you.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.180
Y-You're...

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:32.280
Theodor's so lucky.

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:36.230
I haven't been to Berlin in forever!

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:38.450
Same here, Anett.

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:41.070
Maybe I'll never get to go again.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.020
There are a hundred thousand BETAs.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:45.020
I-It'll be fine.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:48.060
If we all work together, 
we can defeat the BETA for sure.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.370
That's right!

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:51.510
Don't get down!

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.030
Y-Yeah.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.040
What's wrong, Anett?

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.180
Sorry, sorry!

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:01.120
I was just thinking about the future.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:07.680
So you also suspect me, don't you?

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:10.580
That I'm a Stasi dog...

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.400
That I might betray you at any moment...

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:15.560
O-Oh, come on, Lise!

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.710
I know you're not.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:20.230
You're one of us! Yeah!

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.250
Th-That's right.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:24.730
You saved my life.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.730
Thank you.

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.770
Hey, don't cry, okay?

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:39.000
Commissioner of the Western Theatre Training 
Forces, Major General Franz Heim...

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:42.250
What do you need from us?

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:48.000
I've come to tell you that you aren't the 
only ones trying to fight the Stasi.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.200
Our best officers have been arrested,

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:57.260
and the NPA no longer has the 
power to resist the Stasi.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:01.270
They will use this opportunity 
to initiate a coup d'état.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:04.270
With a huge BETA echelon approaching?

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:08.560
They're taking advantage of the fact 
that the army is on the front lines.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.650
If they can take control of the parliament, 
they can do what they like.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:13.110
Damn.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:17.300
The Western Theatre forces intend to stop them.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:21.290
And you want our help?

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:26.700
We both want to save the people and the nation.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:35.160
We want your help, 
heroes of the Schwarzesmarken.

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:41.310
A Stasi coup d'état?

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:46.020
Perhaps Captain Bernhard knew about this...

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:48.820
<i>And now, an announcement from 
the Ministry of Defense.</i>

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:52.320
<i>The BETA forces that appeared 
from the Minsk hive</i>

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:55.170
<i>appear to be crossing through Poland.</i>

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:56.800
<i>The size of this BETA force is...</i>

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:57.820
They're here?

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:02.610
It'll be two or three days before 
the first wave hits the border.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:04.950
You head back to base.

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.520
I'll remain in Berlin.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:13.200
That last meeting gave us a tiny bit of hope.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.590
Can we trust him?

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:18.740
Major General Heim is a dove.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.600
For him to act means a lot.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:25.460
First, I'll do everything I can to keep 
the squadron in existence.

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.850
That is my fight.

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:30.730
You protect Captain Bernhard.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:34.100
The country needs her.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:38.530
And watch out for your sister.

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.020
If you leave now, you should 
make it back to base by morning.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.600
Hurry.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.250
Comrade Lieutenant!

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.790
Call me "Gretel."

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:50.830
When I'm the only one you keep 
calling "comrade," it's... I mean...

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:53.720
It feels a little sad...

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.300
Make sure you come back, Gretel.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:00.110
O-Of course I will, Theodor Eberbach!

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.320
There you are.

00:18:20.730 --> 00:18:21.780
Lise...

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.080
I've been looking for you.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:24.690
Here.

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:26.150
You dropped this.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:29.570
Sorry, I know I shouldn't have, but...

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.580
I looked inside.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.510
You should be more careful.

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:37.530
If you carry around a photo 
of you and a Westerner,

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:40.250
people will think you're plotting something.

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.300
Y-You're right.

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:44.700
Or...

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.430
Are you?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:52.410
I can tell that my brother and Captain 
Bernhard are planning something...

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:55.140
And that you're involved, Katia.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:19:00.240
If you tell me the truth, 
I think I can protect everyone.

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.360
And if the captain disappears,

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:06.200
you might have a chance, right?

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.860
Lise?

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.010
Theodor!

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:28.220
We made contact with Franz Heim
of the Western Theatre forces.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.440
I see.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.730
You're not surprised.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.490
Now we have a tiny bit of hope.

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:38.520
Yeah, Gretel said the same thing.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:42.420
And we have you to believe in, also.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.320
Me?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:50.500
Because you saved Katia that day, 
we have an extra card in our hand.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.600
A card, huh?

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:56.300
Katia is Lieutenant General 
Strachwitz's daughter.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:59.030
She could bring hope to 
the government opposition.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:03.070
And because you're protecting her,

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:05.840
I can put my full efforts 
into leading the squadron.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:09.890
I'm counting on you.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:19.310
Lise?

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:25.270
You were talking with her a long time, Brother.

00:20:26.340 --> 00:20:29.660
Hey, is there something between 
you and Captain Bernhard?

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:33.710
Are you trying to fight the Stasi?

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:34.730
What are you talking about?!

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:37.670
I was just briefing her on the mission—

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.180
I'm scared...

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.740
The big battle is almost here,

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:45.550
and Katia and Anett still suspect me.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:51.600
Do you think I'm a spy, as well?

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:53.670
You do, right?

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:56.580
You don't know what the Stasi did to me.

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.310
You can't trust me.

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.600
No! You're a part of my family!

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:03.290
I trust you.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.450
Brother...

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:08.720
No one wants to suspect you, either.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:11.450
Are you serious?

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:16.360
I didn't know you had a past like that.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.820
Come with me, Lise Hohenstein.

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:21.210
I'm putting you under arrest.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.660
What are you thinking?

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:25.100
I'm getting rid of uncertainties.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:29.220
She deflects suspicion by bringing 
up how suspicious she is.

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:31.560
That's a common tactic of theirs.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.550
If she were a Stasi pilot, there's a possibility

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:37.060
she was involved in hunting asylum-seekers.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:40.620
Can you allow someone who hunted 
humans in the squadron?

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:41.270
Stop it!

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.770
We're about to fight the BETA.

00:21:43.770 --> 00:21:45.150
If we start losing people...

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.240
I'll back her up!

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:47.950
Anett?

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:50.330
Katia...

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.490
Normally, two members of a family 
aren't put in the same unit.

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:56.620
Unless someone's manipulating things.

00:21:58.090 --> 00:22:00.070
Lise, it's not true, right?

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:01.880
You're not in the Stasi!

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.530
Of course I'm not!

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:05.340
I hate the Stasi!

00:22:05.610 --> 00:22:08.900
After what they did to Mom and Dad,

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:11.390
you also suspect me, Brother!

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:13.530
N-No, I don't... But...

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:17.770
Lise!

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:20.270
Lise!

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:28.530
Lise asked me what the captain is trying to do.

00:22:29.430 --> 00:22:30.780
E-Even so...

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:33.790
You remember your promise, right?

00:22:36.730 --> 00:22:41.650
But even so, I can't abandon her.

00:22:42.410 --> 00:22:43.540
Theodor!

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:55.150
Lise! Lise!

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:04.940
Lise...

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:12.450
Lise? Are you there?

00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:18.280
Lise?

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:23.480
I love you, Brother.

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:28.710
I'd do anything for you.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.030
But I can't do that now.

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:36.630
I can't fight with everyone suspecting me.

00:23:37.330 --> 00:23:38.190
Lise...

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:43.000
But if you believe me...

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:46.320
If you give me something to believe in...

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:51.320
Brother,

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:55.750
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:52.920 --> 00:23:54.020
take me.
